 "indicator": {
  "definition": {
   "definition": "These are the Reserve Bank's direct loans and advances to the Central Government — Ways and Means Advances and any overdue WMA that becomes an overdraft — reported as item 4.1 'Central Government' under 'Loans and Advances' in the WSS 'RBI — Liabilities and Assets' table. Ways and Means Advances are provided by the RBI under Section 17(5) of the Reserve Bank of India Act, 1934, to bridge temporary mismatches between the government's receipts and payments; the limit is set in agreement with the Government, and they are meant to be temporary, so persistent borrowing here is read as a sign of fiscal pressure. This item covers the Central Government only; the State Government counterpart is a separate line.",
   "source_name": "RBI Act, 1934, s. 17(5) (per RBI's published WMA documentation); RBI — Handbook on the WSS, 'RBI – Liabilities and Assets'",
   "source_url": "https://rbidocs.rbi.org.in/rdocs/Publications/PDFs/HWSSF170614.pdf",
   "term": "RBI loans and advances to the Central Government"
  },
